{"version":1,"slug":"Others__Quantitative_Aptitude_-_Arithmetic_-_Number_System_-_SSC_SUPER_PRACTICE_37520_(20Q)","path":"Others/Quantitative Aptitude - Arithmetic - Number System - SSC SUPER PRACTICE 37520 (20Q).html","title":"devgagan","provider":"Others","category":"Quantitative Aptitude - Arithmetic - Number System - SSC SUPER PRACTICE 37520 (20Q).html","durationMinutes":60,"totalQuestions":20,"sectionsLocked":false,"sections":null,"questions":[{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Find the number of common factors of 144, 216 and 288.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>144, 216 &#2324;&#2352; 288 &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2357; &#2327;&#2369;&#2339;&#2344;&#2326;&#2306;&#2337;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">72</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">72</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">24</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">24</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">12</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">12</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">18</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">18</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>The HCF of these numbers is 72 and the number of factors of 72 (2<sup>3</sup> x 3<sup>2</sup>) is 4 x 3 = 12.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>If N = A<sup>2</sup> x B<sup>2</sup> x C<sup>4</sup>, where A, B and C are prime numbers. How many factors of N are perfect squares?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; N = A<sup>2</sup> x B<sup>2</sup> x C<sup>4</sup>, &#2332;&#2361;&#2366;&#2305; A, B &#2324;&#2352; C &#2309;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; N &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2327;&#2369;&#2339;&#2344;&#2326;&#2306;&#2337; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">8</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">8</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">6</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">6</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">10</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">10</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">12</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">12</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>For the factors to be perfect squares, assume A<sup>2</sup> = P, B<sup>2</sup> = Q and C<sup>2</sup>= R</p> <p>So, for the factors to be perfect square, we can write N = PQR<sup>2</sup> = (1+1) (1+1) (2+1) = 12</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>How many factors of 2<sup>4</sup> * 3<sup>2</sup> * 5<sup>7</sup> * 7<sup>3</sup> are divisible by 42 but not by 84?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>2<sup>4</sup> * 3<sup>2</sup> * 5<sup>7</sup> * 7<sup>3</sup> &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2327;&#2369;&#2339;&#2344;&#2326;&#2306;&#2337; 42 &#2360;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2354;&#2375;&#2325;&#2367;&#2344; 84 &#2360;&#2375; &#2344;&#2361;&#2368;&#2306;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">48</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">48</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">24</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">24</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">36</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">36</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">12</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">12</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>42 = 2 * 3 * 7</p><p>84 = 2<sup>2</sup> * 3 * 7</p><p>Now, to have number divisible by 42 and not by 84. We have to make sure that 2 is taken only once. As, if we pick 2 two's, then it will form 84 with no. of 3 and 7 selected and since minimum 3 and 7 we have to select is 1, we cannot have 2 more than one.</p><p>Number= 2<sup>4</sup> * 3<sup>2</sup> * 5<sup>7</sup> * 7<sup>3</sup></p><p>So, there are 2 ways of picking 3, 8 ways of picking 3, 3 ways of picking 7 and only one way of picking 2 and that is 2<sup>1</sup>.</p><p>So, total number of ways = 1 * 2 * 8 * 3 = 48</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>What is the LCM of &#8731;1728, &#8732;256, &radic;196, (32)<sup>1/5</sup></p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#8731;1728, &#8732;256, &radic;196, (32)<sup>1/5</sup> &#2325;&#2366; LCM &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">84</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">84</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">86</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">86</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">168</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">168</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">42</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">42</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>&#8731;1728 = 12 = 2 * 2 * 3</p><p>&#8732;256 = 4 = 2 * 2</p><p>&radic;196 = 14 = 2 * 7</p><p>(32)<sup>1/5</sup> = 2 = 2</p><p>LCM = 2 * 2 * 3 * 7 = 84</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Four bells toll once every 8 seconds, 10 seconds, 15 seconds and 27 seconds respectively. If all the bells together toll at 7:00 am, then they will toll together next at -</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2330;&#2366;&#2352; &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2305; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; &#2361;&#2352; 8 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;, 10 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;, 15 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337; &#2324;&#2352; 27 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2366;&#2352; &#2348;&#2332;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2360;&#2349;&#2368; &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2305; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2360;&#2369;&#2348;&#2361; 7:00 &#2348;&#2332;&#2375; &#2348;&#2332;&#2375;&#2306;&#2327;&#2368;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2357;&#2375; &#2309;&#2327;&#2354;&#2368; &#2348;&#2366;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2348;&#2332;&#2375;&#2306;&#2327;&#2368; -</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">7:18 am</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">7:18 &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2361;&#2381;&#2344;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">7.05 am</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2360;&#2369;&#2348;&#2361; 7.05 &#2348;&#2332;&#2375;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">7:20 am</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">7:20 &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2361;&#2381;&#2344;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">7:15 am</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">7:15 &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2361;&#2381;&#2344;</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>LCM of 8, 10, 15 and 27 = 1080 s = 18 minutes</p><p>Required time = 7:00 am + 18 minutes = 7:18 am</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Products of two numbers is 7134. If HCF of the numbers is 58, then LCM of numbers is : </p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2327;&#2369;&#2339;&#2344;&#2347;&#2354; 7134 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; HCF 58 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; LCM &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">93</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">93</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">113</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">113</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">143</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">143</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">123</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">123</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>LCM * HCF = Product of two numbers</p><p>LCM * 58 = 7134</p><p>LCM = 7134/58 </p><p>LCM = 123</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>HCF and products of numbers are 5 and 1050 respectively. The number of possible pairs of numbers are : </p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; HCF &#2324;&#2352; &#2327;&#2369;&#2339;&#2344;&#2347;&#2354; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 5 &#2324;&#2352; 1050 &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2306;&#2349;&#2366;&#2357;&#2367;&#2340; &#2351;&#2369;&#2327;&#2381;&#2350;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;: </p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">1</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">3</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">3</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">2</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">2</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">4</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">4</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>Let the numbers are 5a and 5b respectively</p><p>According to question,</p><p>5a * 5b = 1050</p><p>ab = 42</p><p>required possible pair of values of a and b which are prime to each other are (7, 6), (14 * 3), (21 * 2), (1 * 42)</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>LCM of two numbers is 12 times of the HCF of the numbers and sum of LCM and HCF of numbers is 208. If one number is 48, then find the other number.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; LCM &#2313;&#2344; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; HCF &#2325;&#2366; 12 &#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; LCM &#2324;&#2352; HCF &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327; 208 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 48 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">44</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">44</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">46</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">46</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">64</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">64</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">54</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">54</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>Let the other number be a and HCF of numbers be x</p><p>Then LCM of numbers = 12x</p><p>According to question,</p><p>x + 12x = 208</p><p>x = 208/13 = 16</p><p>LCM = 16 * 12 = 192</p><p>LCM * HCF = Products of two numbers</p><p>16 * 192 = 48 * a</p><p>a = (16 * 192)/48</p><p>a = 64</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>HCF and LCM of two numbers are 21 and 2457 respectively. If one number lies between 170 to 200, then the number is : </p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; HCF &#2324;&#2352; LCM &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 21 &#2324;&#2352; 2457 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 170 &#2360;&#2375; 200 &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2357;&#2361; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;: </p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">183</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">183</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">175</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">175</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">199</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">199</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">189</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">189</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>Let the numbers are 21a and 21b </p><p>LCM * HCF = product of two numbers</p><p>21 * 2457 = 21a * 21b</p><p>ab = (21 * 2457)/(21 * 21)</p><p>ab = 117</p><p>Two co- prime numbers with product 117 are 13 and 9</p><p>Therefore, the required number is (21 * 13, 21 * 9) = 273 and 189</p><p>Number which lies between 170 to 200 = 189</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Find the least number which when divided by 8, 13, 26 and 52 leaves remainder of 3 in each case.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2357;&#2361; &#2360;&#2348;&#2360;&#2375; &#2331;&#2379;&#2335;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2375; 8, 13, 26 &#2324;&#2352; 52 &#2360;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340;&#2367; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359; 3 &#2348;&#2330;&#2375;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">107</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">107</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">102</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">102</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">97</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">97</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">112</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">112</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>LCM of 8, 13, 26 and 52 is 104</p><p>Required number = 104 + 3 = 107</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Find the greatest five-digit number which is exactly divisible by 4, 7 and 12.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2346;&#2366;&#2305;&#2330; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2361; &#2360;&#2348;&#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319; &#2332;&#2379; 4, 7 &#2324;&#2352; 12 &#2360;&#2375; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339;&#2340;&#2307; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; &#2361;&#2379;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">99960</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">99960</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">99964</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">99964</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">99978</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">99978</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">99984</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">99984</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>Greatest 5  -  digit number = 99999</p><p>LCM of 4, 7 and 12 = 84</p><p>99999 when divided by 84 leaves 39 as remainder</p><p>Required number = 99999  -  39 = 99960</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Find the greatest five  -  digit number which when divided by 3, 4, 6 and 15 leaves remainder of 1 in each case.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2346;&#2366;&#2306;&#2330; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2361; &#2360;&#2348;&#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2375; 3, 4, 6 &#2324;&#2352; 15 &#2360;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340;&#2367; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 1 &#2358;&#2375;&#2359; &#2348;&#2330;&#2375;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">99935</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">99935</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">99961</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">99961</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">99960</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">99960</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">99984</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">99984</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>Greatest 5  -  digit number = 99999</p><p>LCM of 3, 4, 6 and 15 = 60</p><p>99999 when divided by 60 leaves 39 as remainder</p><p>Required number = 99999  -  39 + 1 = 99961</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>HCF and LCM of two numbers are 13 and 156 respectively. If one of the two numbers are 26, then find the other number.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; HCF &#2324;&#2352; LCM &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 13 &#2324;&#2352; 156 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; 26 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">70</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">70</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">64</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">64</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">78</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">78</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">88</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">88</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>Let the other number = b</p><p>LCM * HCF = Product of two numbers</p><p>13 * 156 = 26 * b</p><p>b = (13 * 156)/26</p><p>b = 78</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>A and B are two prime numbers such that A &gt; B and their LCM is 667. Find the value of B - A + 2AB.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2342;&#2379; &#2309;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2332;&#2376;&#2360;&#2375; A &gt; B &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2366; LCM 667 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; B - A + 2AB &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">1338</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1338</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">1328</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1328</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">1342</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1342</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">1314</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1314</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>Prime factors of 667 is 23 and 29</p><p>A = 29</p><p>B = 23</p><p>B  -  A + 2AB = 23  -  29 + 2 * 23 * 29 </p><p>=&gt; 1328</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>a, b, c and 23 are four distinct number and the HCF of each pair of numbers (23, a) ; (23, b) ; (23, c) is 23 where a, b, c are each less than 95 and a &lt; b &lt; c. what is the value of </p><p>(b * c + a)/2</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>a, b, c &#2324;&#2352; 23 &#2330;&#2366;&#2352; &#2309;&#2354;&#2327;-&#2309;&#2354;&#2327; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2332;&#2379;&#2337;&#2364;&#2375; (23, a) ; (23, b) ; (23, c) &#2325;&#2366; HCF 23 &#2361;&#2376; &#2332;&#2361;&#2366;&#2305; a, b, c &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; 95 &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2350; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; a &lt; b &lt; c. &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p><p>(b * c + a)/2</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">3095</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">3095</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">3145</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">3145</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">3244</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">3244</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">3197</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">3197</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>The four distinct numbers are 23, a, b and c</p><p>HCF is always the factor of the given numbers</p><p>a, b, c should be multiple of 23 as the HCF is 23</p><p>Only possible multiples of a, b and c is 2, 3 and 4 respectively</p><p>As a, b and c each are less than 95</p><p>So, a = 23 * 2 = 46</p><p>b = 23 * 3 = 69</p><p>c = 23 * 4 = 92</p><p>(b * c + a)/2 = (69 * 92 + 46)/2 </p><p>=&gt; (6348 + 46)/2 = 6394/2</p><p>=&gt; 3197</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Find the largest 4  -  digit number which when divided by 5, 6 and 7 leaves remainder of 1, 2 and 3 respectively.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>4 &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2348;&#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2375; 5, 6 &#2324;&#2352; 7 &#2360;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 1, 2 &#2324;&#2352; 3 &#2358;&#2375;&#2359; &#2348;&#2330;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">9967</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">9967</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">9866</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">9866</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">9935</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">9935</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">9845</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">9845</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>Largest 4  -  digit number = 9999</p><p>LCM of 5, 6 and 7 = 210</p><p>Common remainder = (5  -  1) = (6  -  2) = (7  -  3) = 4</p><p>Remainder when 9999 divided by 210 = 129</p><p>Required number = 9999  -  129  -  4 = 9866</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The greatest number which divides 208, 258 and 308 leaves remainder 8 in each case.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2357;&#2361; &#2360;&#2348;&#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2379; 208, 258 &#2324;&#2352; 308 &#2325;&#2379; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340;&#2367; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359; 8 &#2331;&#2379;&#2337;&#2364;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">125</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">125</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">50</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">50</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">25</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">25</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">75</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">75</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>The required number will be HCF of (208  -  8), (258  -  8) and (308  -  8) = 200, 250 and 300</p><p>HCF of 200, 250 and 300 = 50</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>A milkman has three different qualities of milk. 517 gallons of 1st quality, 611 gallons of 2nd quality and 706 gallons of 3rd quality. Find the least possible number of bottles of equal size in which different milk of different qualities can be filled without mixing.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343;&#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2366;&#2360; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2309;&#2354;&#2327;-&#2309;&#2354;&#2327; &#2325;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2367;&#2335;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2346;&#2361;&#2354;&#2368; &#2325;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2367;&#2335;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; 517 &#2327;&#2376;&#2354;&#2344;, &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2368; &#2325;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2367;&#2335;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; 611 &#2327;&#2376;&#2354;&#2344; &#2324;&#2352; &#2340;&#2368;&#2360;&#2352;&#2368; &#2325;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2367;&#2335;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; 706 &#2327;&#2376;&#2354;&#2344;&#2404; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2310;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2348;&#2379;&#2340;&#2354;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2350; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2350; &#2360;&#2306;&#2349;&#2366;&#2357;&#2367;&#2340; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2309;&#2354;&#2327;-&#2309;&#2354;&#2327; &#2325;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2367;&#2335;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2354;&#2327;-&#2309;&#2354;&#2327; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2348;&#2367;&#2344;&#2366; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2319; &#2349;&#2352;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366; &#2360;&#2325;&#2375;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">39</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">39</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">37</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">37</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">41</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">41</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">33</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">33</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>First quality = 517 Gallons, Second quality = 611 Gallons, Third quality = 705 Gallons</p><p>The least number of bottles will be in the size of HCF of 517, 611, and 705.</p><p>Now,</p><p>517 = 47 x 11</p><p>611 = 47 x 13</p><p>705 = 47 x 15</p><p>HCF = 47</p><p>So, required number of bottles = 11 + 13 + 15 = 39</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>If the number of even factors and odd factors of 440 is X and Y, then find the value of Y/X.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 440 &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350; &#2327;&#2369;&#2339;&#2344;&#2326;&#2306;&#2337;&#2379;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2357;&#2367;&#2359;&#2350; &#2327;&#2369;&#2339;&#2344;&#2326;&#2306;&#2337;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; X &#2324;&#2352; Y &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; Y/X &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">3</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">3</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">1/3</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1/3</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">4</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">4</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">2</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">2</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>440 = 2 x 2 x 2 x 5 x 11 = 2<sup>3</sup> x 5<sup>1</sup> x 11<sup>1</sup></p><p>Number of odd factors (leave the 2's) = (1 + 1) x (1 + 1) = 4 = X</p><p>Number of even factors = number of 2's x (1 + 1) x (1 + 1) = 12 = Y</p><p>Therefore,</p><p>Y/X = 12/4 = 3</p><p></p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Find the HCF of 7, 2.8, and 0.14.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>7, 2.8 &#2324;&#2352; 0.14 &#2325;&#2366; HCF &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">0.7</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">0.7</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">0.14</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">0.14</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">1.4</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1.4</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">7</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">7</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>We can write 7, 2.8, and 0.14 as 7.00, 2.80, and 0.14 respectively.</p><p>After leaving the decimals, we have 700, 280, and 14.</p><p>And 700 and 280 both are divisible by 14.</p><p>Therefore, the required HCF (with added decimal) will be 0.14.</p><p></p>","marks":2,"section":null}]}